      en: "Český Šternberk Castle is a Gothic castle in the Sázava River valley. It was built in the mid-13th century by Zdeslav of Sternberg. The castle features a tall tower and a drawbridge. It houses a museum of the Sternberg family history, with exhibits of armor, coins, and art. The castle has never been conquered by force. It remains in private ownership and is open to the public. The castle's location offers panoramic views of the surrounding countryside.",
