      en: "The city fortifications of Kroměříž were built in the 13th century and later expanded several times. The town was the seat of the Bishops of Olomouc, so the fortifications had special importance. The wall enclosed the old town and the bishop's chateau. In the 17th century, the fortifications were repaired after damage in the Thirty Years' War. Today, only remnants of the wall and the Zderad Gate survive. The fortifications bear witness to episcopal power.",
